%% Class Diagram: Result Type Hierarchy and Pipeline Behaviors
%% Based on Chapter 7 — Detailed Design

classDiagram
    class Result~T~ {
        +bool IsSuccess
        +bool IsFailure
        +int StatusCode
        +List~Error~ Errors
        +T? Value
        +ToResult() IResult
    }

    class Result {
        +bool IsSuccess$
        +bool IsFailure$
        +int StatusCode$
        +List~Error~ Errors$
        +Created~T~(T value) Result~T~$
        +Ok~T~(T value) Result~T~$
        +NotFound(string code) Result$
        +Conflict(string code) Result$
        +Validation(string code) Result$
        +Unexpected(string code) Result$
    }

    class Error {
        +string Code
        +string Message
        +ErrorType Type
        +Dictionary~string,object~? Metadata
        +implicit operator Result(Error error)
    }

    class PagedResult~T~ {
        +List~T~ Data
        +int PageNumber
        +int PageSize
        +int TotalCount
        +int TotalPages
        +bool HasPreviousPage
        +bool HasNextPage
    }

    class IPipelineBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~ {
        <<interface>>
        +Handle(TRequest, RequestHandlerDelegate~TResponse~) Task~TResponse~
    }

    class LoggingBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~ {
        +Handle(...) Task~TResponse~
    }

    class ValidationBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~ {
        -IValidator[] validators
        +Handle(...) Task~TResponse~
    }

    class ExceptionMappingBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~ {
        +Handle(...) Task~TResponse~
    }

    class ICommand~TResponse~ {
        <<interface>>
    }

    class IQuery~TResponse~ {
        <<interface>>
    }

    class ICommandHandler~TCommand,TResponse~ {
        <<interface>>
        +Handle(TCommand, CancellationToken) Task~TResponse~
    }

    class IQueryHandler~TQuery,TResponse~ {
        <<interface>>
        +Handle(TQuery, CancellationToken) Task~TResponse~
    }

    Result~T~ --> Result : uses factory methods
    Result --> Error : contains
    Result~T~ --> PagedResult~T~ : specialization
    Error --> Result : implicit conversion
    IPipelineBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~ <|-- LoggingBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~
    IPipelineBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~ <|-- ValidationBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~
    IPipelineBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~ <|-- ExceptionMappingBehavior~TRequest,TResponse~
    ICommandHandler~TCommand,TResponse~ ..> ICommand~TResponse~ : processes
    IQueryHandler~TQuery,TResponse~ ..> IQuery~TResponse~ : processes
```

## Diagram Description

The class diagram shows the two most important type hierarchies in the system:

1. **Result / Error types** — The `Result<T>` and `Error` types form the core of the explicit error-handling strategy. `Error` has an implicit conversion to `Result`, enabling handlers to return `Error` directly without wrapping it.
2. **Pipeline behaviors** — The Decorator pattern implementation via MediatR's `IPipelineBehavior`. Each behavior wraps the next, forming a chain of responsibility.

**Evidence**: `Shared/Application/Models/Results/Result.cs`, `Shared/Application/Models/Errors/Error.cs`, `Shared/Application/Mediators/Behaviours/`
